A||N||4||rhauser||Headlight Motors - I've tried everything||||1||
Z||000000||rhauser||06-21-2001||11:36 AM||||My headlight motors on the 85GT are acting really weird...<P>The drivers side (which was the first to stop working) is functioning fine.  However the passenger side will not go up unless I open the hood and turn the knob a little.  While it is up it makes a period "clicking" noise and the headlight dims a bit while the motor clicks. When I turn them off the passenger side stays up for a few seconds and then drops normally.<P>I have replaced the motor twice with rebuilt motors and also I hane replaced all three relays.<P>Any ideas?<P>Thanks in advance - Rob||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_24||06-21-2001||11:41 AM||||Check the ground to it.  I had a similar problem on my old Sport Coupe and you would have to hold the headlamp button half way down until they went up, then push the button the rest of the way in.  <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||rhauser||06-21-2001||03:21 PM||||Do you mean the ground to the switch on the dash or to the headlight motor?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||06-21-2001||05:24 PM||||Oil the pivot points (or hinges if you will)they rust up, I had that problem on my 85 and I oiled them up and put a little grease where the small torsion rodswhere they contact, it helped alot.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||06-22-2001||10:08 AM||||Check the ground at the switch with a wire tester at the switch and at the motor.  I am not sure if they are the same ground or not.  Mine was bad near the motor, the ground was all coroded.  Hope this helps a little.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
